@startuml lighting
package environment {
  class Lighting {
    - gameWindow: window.GameWindow
    - darknessFilter: java.awt.image.BufferedImage
    + Lighting(gameWindow: window.GameWindow, circleSize: int)
    + draw(g2: java.awt.Graphics2D): void
  }

  class EnvironmentManager {
    - gameWindow: window.GameWindow
    - lighting: Lighting
    + EnvironmentManager(gameWindow: window.GameWindow)
    + setUp(): void
    + draw(g2: java.awt.Graphics2D): void
  }
}

package frame {
  class FrameApp {
    + getScreenWidth(): int
    + getScreenHeight(): int
    + getTileSize(): int
  }
}

package window {
  class GameWindow {
    + getPlayer(): Player
  }

  class Player {
    + getScreenX(): int
    + getScreenY(): int
  }
}

EnvironmentManager "1" *-- "0..1" Lighting : manages
Lighting ..> FrameApp : uses (static methods)
Lighting ..> GameWindow : reads player position
Lighting ..> Player : calls getScreenX/Y
GameWindow "1" o-- "0..1" Player : has

note right of Lighting
**Notes**
- 画面全体を暗くする BufferedImage を保持し、プレイヤー周囲を円形に透明化して明るくする。
- 中心座標は player.getScreenX() / getScreenY() に tileSize/2 を加えて計算する。
- AlphaComposite.Clear で円をくり抜く実装。画面サイズやプレイヤー移動時に再生成が必要。

- Holds a BufferedImage darkness filter that darkens the entire screen and makes the area around the player circularly bright.
- The center coordinates are calculated by adding tileSize/2 to player.getScreenX() and player.getScreenY().
- Implements the circle cutout using AlphaComposite.Clear; the filter should be regenerated when screen size or player position changes.
end note

note right of EnvironmentManager
**Notes**
- setUp() は Lighting インスタンスを初期化します。
- draw() はオーバーレイを描画するために Lighting.draw を呼び出します。

- setUp() initializes the Lighting instance.
- draw() calls Lighting.draw to render the overlay.
end note

@enduml